  "question": {
    "text": "If $f(x)=\\frac{3 x-4}{2 x-3}$, then $f(f(f(x)))$ will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "x",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 x$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2 x-3}{3 x-4}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{3 x-4}{2 x-3}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(x)=\\frac{3 x-4}{2 x-3}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\nf(f(f(x))) & =f\\left(f\\left(\\frac{3 x-4}{2 x-3}\\right)\\right) \\\\\n& =f\\left(\\frac{3\\left(\\frac{3 x-4}{2 x-3}\\right)-4}{2\\left(\\frac{3 x-4}{2 x-3}\\right)-3}\\right)=f(x)\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}